Bug 2083485 - Don't give the calendar password to a proxy during CalDAV and ICS detection. r=tobyp

The detection sessions checked only channel.URI before handing out the
password. On a proxy challenge that URI is still the origin, so the
proxy got the origin credentials. Refuse challenges flagged AUTH_PROXY.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337946

diff --git a/calendar/providers/caldav/modules/CalDavSession.sys.mjs b/calendar/providers/caldav/modules/CalDavSession.sys.mjs
--- a/calendar/providers/caldav/modules/CalDavSession.sys.mjs
+++ b/calendar/providers/caldav/modules/CalDavSession.sys.mjs
@@ -153,9 +153,12 @@ export class CalDavDetectionSession exte
   /**
    * @see {nsIAuthPrompt2}
    */
   promptAuth(aChannel, aLevel, aAuthInfo) {
-    if (!this.password) {
+    // FIXME: Proxies that ask for Basic or Digest credentials can't be used
+    // for detection. NTLM and Negotiate proxies are answered by necko with the
+    // system credentials and never get here.
+    if (!this.password || aAuthInfo.flags & Ci.nsIAuthInformation.AUTH_PROXY) {
       return false;
     }
 
     if ((aAuthInfo.flags & aAuthInfo.PREVIOUS_FAILED) == 0) {
